# antseal golden-vector freeze manifest — format version v1  (task Q6)
#
# Two guarantees in one file:
#
#   1. FREEZE   — every listed digest pins the exact bytes of a committed
#                 vector file. Editing or deleting one turns CI red.
#   2. MUST-EXIST — the list of hash lines *is* the must-exist list: the
#                 runner can only fail on files it finds, so a deleted file
#                 is invisible to it and is caught here instead. Vectors
#                 the M0 freeze still owes are declared as `#! pending`
#                 below, each naming the task that must land it.
#
# Only committed vector files (*.json) are frozen. Auxiliaries — README.md
# and the `*.py` reference generators — are deliberately NOT frozen: the
# generators are re-runnable cross-checks, and the JSON they produced is
# what the format actually commits to.
#
# This file is `sha256sum -c` compatible (lines starting with `#` are
# comments to GNU coreutils), so the digests can be checked with a tool
# that shares no code with antseal:
#
#     cd testdata/vectors/v1 && grep -v '^#' FROZEN.sha256 | sha256sum -c -
#
# The authoritative checker is `crates/antseal-core/tests/vector_freeze.rs`
# (CI lane `vector-freeze`, driver `scripts/vector-freeze.sh`). Regenerate
# with `scripts/vector-freeze.sh --update`. Contract + retention policy:
# `testdata/vectors/README.md`, `testdata/README.md`.
#
# ── directives (`#!`), parsed by the checker ────────────────────────────
#
#   manifest-version  this file's own schema version
#   format-version    the vector format version; MUST equal the directory
#   status            pre-freeze | frozen   (see below)
#   freeze-gate       the task that flips `status` to `frozen`
#   kind <name> <since>   a vector kind that freezes with this version;
#                     the set must equal test_util::vectors::KNOWN_KINDS
#   pending <slug> <task> <what it must pin>
#                     a must-exist vector this version still owes
#
# `status pre-freeze` (today): vectors may still be regenerated, moved, or
# re-containered as a recorded, justified change — re-run `--update` and
# review the digest diff. `status frozen` (set by Q14): digests are
# permanent, `--update` refuses to modify or drop an entry, additions are
# the only legal change, and `pending` must be empty.
#
#! manifest-version 1
#! format-version v1
#! status frozen
#! freeze-gate Q14
#
# Frozen vector kinds (kind name + payload shape freeze at Q14; the Q4
# envelope itself is shared and versioned separately by `schema_version`).
#
#! kind hkdf-labels C3
#! kind commitments C16
#! kind unit-aead C16
#! kind manifest-aead C16
#! kind signatures C16
#! kind sig-reject C15
#! kind fine-tree G15
#! kind content-model G21
#! kind report R9
#! kind manifest F12
#! kind bundle F13
#
# ADDED 2026-08-01 (S4), post-freeze: the `storage-address` kind — the D32
# address rule (BLAKE3-256 of the blob bytes) over the S4 size ladder, with
# cap + 1 committed as a typed REJECTION. A post-freeze kind addition is the
# sanctioned append path (the same one the M2 `anchor` kind is reserved
# for): new `#! kind` line + new digest line; no existing digest moves.
#! kind storage-address S4
#
# ADDED 2026-08-09 (A22), post-freeze: the `anchor` kind — the reservation
# named at line 69 above, taken up. It pins the whole per-anchor verdict
# object (state, headline eligibility, verified time, source, fetch date,
# diagnostic, identity discriminant, the A39 suppressed list and the R12
# report slot) for seven cases over four recorded artifacts, at a fixed
# `verify_at` against `TsaRootStore::pinned()`. Same append path as S4
# executed on 2026-08-01: new `#! kind` line + new digest line, no existing
# digest moved, no existing vector touched.
#
# `anchor` is the SECOND kind whose bytes are a function of the VERIFIER
# rather than of the format (D94 §2a). The D94 verdict-event escape in
# `scripts/vector-freeze.sh` is scoped to `report/` **by path** and does not
# reach it, so an `anchor` vector cannot legally move. The three events that
# could ever require one — an A26 root REMOVAL, a signer-DN rendering
# change, and a root append that gives a pinned token a second valid path —
# are listed in D101 §4.3; each needs its own record, which is also where
# `verdict_event_ok` would be extended. None is proposed, and the third is
# measured absent (`chain.rs`'s five-token append test).
#! kind anchor A22
#
# Must-exist vectors this version still owes before Q14 can freeze it.
# Each names its owning task; Q14's gate condition is ZERO pending lines.
#
# ***NONE REMAIN.*** Every must-exist obligation v1 owed has landed, so the
# Q14 gate condition on this file is met: `status frozen` is now refusable
# only for reasons outside the pending set.
#
# LANDED 2026-07-28 (G15), obligation discharged and its `#! pending` line
# deleted with the vector, per the freeze contract: `fine-tree-unbalanced-n6`
# → `fine-tree/fine-tree.json`, the `fine-tree` kind's unbalanced n=6 case
# pinning MSB-first GGM indexing (MVP-SPEC.md line 169).
#
# LANDED 2026-07-28 (R9): `verification-reports` →
# `report/verification-reports.json`, the `report` kind — every M0 shape's
# canonical bundle mapped to the byte-exact serialized VerificationReport
# (MVP-SPEC.md lines 153, 167, 169). It was rostered with
# `must_exist_before_freeze: false`, so it had no `#! pending` line here to
# delete; its INDEX.json `pending` entry moved to `vectors` in the same
# commit.
# LANDED 2026-07-28 (F12), same discharge: `manifest-encode-decode` →
# `manifest/manifest.json`, the `manifest` kind's six works — canonical
# envelope bytes, two-layer diagnostic sidecars, and the work_id/
# anchor_digest each hashes to, which is also where F7's deferred
# committed-digest artifact lands (MVP-SPEC.md lines 75, 153).
#
# LANDED 2026-07-28 (F13), the LAST must-exist obligation: `bundle-empty-anchor`
# → `bundle/bundle.json`, whose `empty-anchor-unanchored` case is the M0
# milestone artifact — a `.sealproof` carrying no OTS artifact, no TSA
# artifact and no receipt, which must decode, round-trip and verify like any
# other (MVP-SPEC.md lines 112-114, 153).
#
# ── frozen digests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
